---
import ArticleClosingNote from "@/components/articles/ArticleClosingNote.astro";
import ArticleImage from "@/components/ui/ArticleImage.astro";
import BentoGrid from "@/components/ui/BentoGrid.astro";

import belfryTower from "@/assets/articles/bruges/belfry-tower-of-bruges.webp";
import bonifaceBridge from "@/assets/articles/bruges/boniface-bridge.webp";
import rozenhoedkaaiSunrise from "@/assets/articles/bruges/bruges-belgium-rozenhoedkaai-sunrise.webp";
import rozenhoedkaaiSunset from "@/assets/articles/bruges/bruges-belgium-rozenhoedkaai-sunset.webp";
import bonifaceCanalView from "@/assets/articles/bruges/bruges-boniface-bridge-canal-view.webp";
import bonifaceChurchView from "@/assets/articles/bruges/boniface-bridge-church-of-our-lady-view-bruges.webp";
import burgSquare from "@/assets/articles/bruges/burg-square-bruges.webp";
import canalView from "@/assets/articles/bruges/bruges-canal-view.webp";
import canalViews from "@/assets/articles/bruges/bruges-canal-views.webp";
import deGastroExterior from "@/assets/articles/bruges/bruges-de-gastro-restaurant.webp";
import marktSquare from "@/assets/articles/bruges/bruges-markt-square.webp";
import minnewater from "@/assets/articles/bruges/bruges-minnewater-the-lake-of-love.webp";
import ottoExterior from "@/assets/articles/bruges/bruges-otto-waffle-atelier.webp";
import chocolateLineShop from "@/assets/articles/bruges/bruges-the-chocolate-line.webp";
import deGastroFood from "@/assets/articles/bruges/de-gastro-restsaurant-bruges.webp";
import ottoWaffle from "@/assets/articles/bruges/otto-waffle-atelier-bruges.webp";
import chocolateLineDisplay from "@/assets/articles/bruges/the-chocolate-line-bruges.webp";
import oldChocolateHouse from "@/assets/articles/bruges/the-old-chocolate-house-bruges.webp";

const prose = "article-prose max-w-3xl text-black/80 [&_p]:mb-5 [&_p:last-child]:mb-0";
---

<section id="section-0" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>1. Explore Markt Square & Climb the Belfry Tower of Bruges</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>The Markt is the heart of Bruges and one of the first places you'll come across when exploring the city.</p>
    <p>Surrounded by colourful historic buildings, cafés, and the iconic Belfry Tower, it's the perfect place to start your day. No matter where I was heading, I somehow always found myself back here.</p>
    <p>If you're planning to climb the Belfry, I'd recommend booking your ticket through the <a href="https://www.museabrugge.be/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#69746E] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#4a534f]">official Musea Brugge website</a> before your visit. During busy periods, tickets can sell out quickly, and choosing an early morning time slot is one of the best ways to avoid the longest queues.</p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 md:gap-4">
      <ArticleImage src={marktSquare} alt="Markt Square in Bruges with colourful guild houses" caption="Markt Square, the beating heart of Bruges" />
      <ArticleImage src={belfryTower} alt="The Belfry Tower of Bruges rising above Markt Square" caption="The Belfry Tower — 366 steps to panoramic views" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-1" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>
      2. Don't miss the most beautiful canal view in Bruges at Rozenhoedkaai
      </h3>
      </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>If you've ever seen a postcard of Bruges, there's a good chance it was taken here.</p>
    <p>Rozenhoedkaai is one of the city's most photographed spots, and it's easy to see why. The canal, the historic buildings, and their reflections on the water create one of the most iconic views in Bruges.</p>
    <p>I visited at sunrise on my first morning in Bruges and came back again around sunset. Seeing the same place at two completely different times of the day gave it a totally different atmosphere.</p>
    <p>I've included both sunrise and sunset photos below because I think they show two very different sides of Rozenhoedkaai. If you have the time, I'd recommend visiting twice. But if I had to choose, sunrise was easily my favourite!</p>
  </div>
    <BentoGrid items={[
      { src: rozenhoedkaaiSunrise, alt: "Rozenhoedkaai canal view at sunrise in Bruges", title: "Sunrise" },
      { src: rozenhoedkaaiSunset, alt: "Rozenhoedkaai canal view at sunset in Bruges", title: "Sunset" },
    ]} />
</section>

<section id="section-2" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>3. Experience the Magic of Boniface Bridge</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>Boniface Bridge is one of those places that instantly made me stop and take out my camera.</p>
    <div class="max-w-md">
      <ArticleImage src={bonifaceBridge} alt="Boniface Bridge over the canal in Bruges" caption="Boniface Bridge — hidden, yet one of the most beautiful spots in Bruges" />
    </div>
    <p>Hidden just below the Church of Our Lady, this small bridge offers one of the most beautiful canal views in Bruges. Even though it's a popular spot, it still feels surprisingly peaceful, especially early in the morning.</p>
    <div class="max-w-md">
      <ArticleImage src={bonifaceChurchView} alt="Church of Our Lady reflected in the canal at Boniface Bridge at sunrise" caption="First light on the Church of Our Lady — one of my favourite photography moments in Bruges" />
    </div>
    <p>I arrived just before sunrise and watched the first light hit the Church of Our Lady in the background. Photos do this place justice, but seeing the light change is something else. I've shared a short video on <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reel/DT-XCCZDFIu/?igsh=MW16Y2hhcDNjM2JvcA==" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#69746E] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#4a534f]">Instagram</a> if you'd like to see it for yourself.</p>
    <p>If you're planning to visit, I'd definitely recommend coming around sunrise. Not only will you avoid the crowds, but you'll also experience this place at its most beautiful.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-3" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>4. Explore Bruges' Canals on Foot</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>One of the best things to do in Bruges is simply walk along its canals.</p>
    <p>Beyond the main squares, you'll discover quiet streets, historic houses, charming stone bridges, and some of the city's most beautiful views. I never followed a specific route and instead wandered wherever the canals led me. Looking back, I wouldn't have explored Bruges any other way.</p>
    <BentoGrid items={[
      { src: canalView, alt: "Walking along the canals in Bruges", title: "Canal-side streets" },
      { src: bonifaceCanalView, alt: "A stone bridge over a canal in Bruges with historic houses", title: "Stone bridges" },
      { src: canalViews, alt: "Canal boat tour passing under a bridge in Bruges", title: "Canal boat tours" },
    ]} />
    <p>If you enjoy seeing a city from the water, I'd also recommend taking a canal cruise. It offers a completely different perspective of Bruges and lets you admire parts of the historic centre you wouldn't normally see on foot. I'd recommend <a href="https://www.getyourguide.com/church-of-our-lady-bruges-l4207?campaign_id=6657346980&adgroup_id=108665649510&target_id=aud-1393039794900:dsa-929853973177&loc_physical_ms=9215685&match_type=&ad_id=450542515401&keyword=&ad_position=&feed_item_id=&placement=&device=c&assetgroup_id=&synthetic_keyword=bruges+canal+tour&partner_id=CD951&gad_source=1&gad_campaignid=6657346980&gclid=Cj0KCQjwjIPSBhCCARIsABGyK7vW87n3HWpS8522CdvOPEFw6mhs_Sy1KF-8mwZlSrjvxwkKz4fPAJ8aApboEALw_wcB" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer sponsored" class="text-[#69746E] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#4a534f]">booking your canal cruise in advance</a>, especially during the busier months.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-4" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>5. Take a Walk Around Minnewater, the Lake of Love</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>If you're looking for a quieter side of Bruges, make some time for a walk around Minnewater, also known as the Lake of Love. Surrounded by trees, walking paths, and calm water, it feels completely different from the busy streets of the historic centre and is one of the most peaceful places to visit in the city.</p>
    <ArticleImage src={minnewater} alt="Minnewater Lake in Bruges, the Lake of Love" caption="Minnewater Lake — one of the most peaceful spots in Bruges" />
    <p>It's only a short walk from the centre, making it an easy stop to add to your itinerary. Take your time, enjoy the views, and if you're lucky, you might even spot a few of Bruges' famous swans along the way.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-5" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>6. Step into Bruges' History at Burg Square</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>Just a short walk from the Markt, Burg Square is home to some of Bruges' most important landmarks, including the impressive City Hall and the Basilica of the Holy Blood.</p>
    <div class="max-w-sm">
      <ArticleImage src={burgSquare} alt="Burg Square in Bruges with the City Hall" caption="Burg Square — home to some of Bruges' most significant historic buildings" />
    </div>
    <p>Even if you're not planning to visit the buildings, it's well worth stopping here for a few minutes. The square has a completely different feel from the Markt, making it one of the best places to admire Bruges' beautiful architecture and history.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-6" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>7. Enjoy a Waffle by the Canal at Otto Waffle Atelier</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>If you're only planning to try one waffle in Bruges, I'd make it this one.</p>
    <p>There are plenty of waffle shops across the city, but Otto Waffle Atelier was the one I kept recommending after my trip. Located right beside the canal, it's the perfect place to stop for breakfast or a coffee break while watching the boats pass by.</p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 md:gap-4">
      <ArticleImage src={ottoExterior} alt="Otto Waffle Atelier beside the canal in Bruges" caption="Otto Waffle Atelier" />
      <ArticleImage src={ottoWaffle} alt="A Belgian waffle from Otto Waffle Atelier in Bruges" caption="Belgian waffle" />
    </div>
    <p>Just keep in mind that this isn't the classic Belgian waffle you'll find elsewhere in Bruges. Otto has created its own take on the traditional waffle using oat flour, giving it a unique twist that's well worth trying.</p>
    <p>If you'd like to try more than one waffle during your trip, you'll also find a few more of my favourite waffle spots <a href="#section-google-map" class="text-[#69746E] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#4a534f]">on the map</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-7" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>8. Try Traditional Belgian Food at De Gastro</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>If I had to recommend just one restaurant in Bruges, it would be <a href="https://www.degastro.be/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#69746E] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#4a534f]">De Gastro</a>.</p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 md:gap-4">
      <ArticleImage src={deGastroFood} alt="Flemish beef stew with fries at De Gastro in Bruges" caption="De Gastro" />
      <ArticleImage src={deGastroExterior} alt="De Gastro restaurant in Bruges" caption="Flemish beef stew" />
    </div>
    <p>I ordered the Flemish beef stew, while my husband went for the steak tartare. Both dishes were excellent and exactly what we were hoping to try during our trip to Belgium.</p>
    <p>The atmosphere is warm, the service was great, and the portions are generous. If you're planning to have dinner here, I'd recommend making a reservation in advance, especially during the busier months.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-8" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>9. Experience Belgian Hot Chocolate at The Old Chocolate House</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>I wasn't expecting a cup of hot chocolate to become one of my favourite memories from Bruges, but that's exactly what happened.</p>
    <p>What makes this place so special is that you don't simply order a hot chocolate – you get to make it yourself. Depending on the flavour you choose, you'll be served a cup of hot milk alongside a handmade chocolate cup filled with matching chocolates and toppings. Simply pour everything into the milk, stir, and watch it melt into your own rich Belgian hot chocolate.</p>
    <ArticleImage src={oldChocolateHouse} alt="The Old Chocolate House in Bruges" caption="The Old Chocolate House — one of the most popular spots in Bruges" />
    <p>I chose the praline version, while my husband went for the Baileys hot chocolate. By the time we left, we were already talking about coming back to try another flavour.</p>
    <p>Before you leave, don't miss the chocolate shop next door, where you can pick up many of the same handmade chocolates to take home.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-9" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>10. Treat Yourself to Belgian Pralines at The Chocolate Line</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>Don't leave Bruges without stopping by The Chocolate Line.</p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 md:gap-4">
      <ArticleImage src={chocolateLineShop} alt="The Chocolate Line shop in Bruges" caption="The Chocolate Line" />
      <ArticleImage src={chocolateLineDisplay} alt="Display of pralines at The Chocolate Line in Bruges" caption="Praline selection" />
    </div>
    <p>Unlike many traditional chocolate shops, this one is known for experimenting with unexpected flavours while staying true to Belgian chocolate craftsmanship. One of the things I loved most was that you can build your own box of pralines, making it easy to try a variety of flavours.</p>
    <p>My favourite was the Defender praline, filled with hazelnut praline and popping candy. The crackling texture instantly reminded me of the sweets I used to eat as a child, and it ended up being one of the most memorable chocolates I tried in Bruges.</p>
    <p>If you'd like to bring home more Belgian chocolates, you'll also find a few more of my favourite chocolate shops <a href="#section-google-map" class="text-[#69746E] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#4a534f]">on the map</a>. If you're curious about the different praline flavours, you can browse their full collection on the <a href="https://www.thechocolateline.be/nl/p/assortiment" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#69746E] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#4a534f]">official Chocolate Line website</a> before your visit.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-10" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>Where to Stay in Bruges</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>If it's your first time in Bruges, I'd recommend staying within walking distance of the historic centre. The city is very walkable, and you'll be able to reach all the places mentioned in this guide on foot.</p>
    <p>During my stay, I chose <a href="https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Grand+Hotel+Casselbergh+Bruges" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#69746E] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#4a534f]">Grand Hotel Casselbergh</a> and would happily stay there again. Its location made it incredibly easy to explore Bruges on foot, while the beautifully decorated lounges gave the hotel so much character. The breakfast buffet was excellent, and the spa became my favourite place to unwind after a full day of exploring Bruges.</p>
    <p>If you're looking for a few more options, here are a few other hotels I'd consider staying at on my next visit to Bruges.</p>
    <h4 class="mb-2 text-black">Luxury Stay</h4>
    <p><a href="https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Dukes%27+Palace+Bruges" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#69746E] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#4a534f]">Dukes' Palace</a> – One of the most iconic luxury hotels in Bruges, housed in a former ducal palace just a short walk from the Markt.</p>
    <h4 class="mb-2 mt-6 text-black">Boutique Hotel</h4>
    <p><a href="https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=The+Pand+Hotel+Bruges" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#69746E] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#4a534f]">The Pand Hotel</a> – An elegant boutique hotel in the heart of Bruges, known for its cosy atmosphere, personalised service, and beautifully designed rooms.</p>
    <h4 class="mb-2 mt-6 text-black">Romantic Canal Stay</h4>
    <p><a href="https://www.booking.com/searchresults.html?ss=Hotel+De+Orangerie+Bruges" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#69746E] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#4a534f]">Hotel De Orangerie</a> – A charming canal-side boutique hotel that's perfect for couples looking for a romantic stay in one of Bruges' most picturesque locations.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-11" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
    <h3>FAQ</h3>
  </div>
  <div class={`${prose} space-y-6`}>
    <div id="faq-0" class="scroll-mt-nav">
      <h4 class="mb-2 text-black">1. How to get to Bruges?</h4>
      <p>The easiest way to get to Bruges is by train, especially if you're travelling from Brussels. There are frequent connections throughout the day, and the journey usually takes around one hour.</p>
      <p>If you're travelling by train, I'd recommend checking routes and booking your tickets through <a href="https://www.omio.com/?clickid=yVuTIZyRnxyZW5uwC2xuzTIBUkuQEoxW%3AUJ7040&irgwc=1&afsrc=1&utm_campaign=1141115&utm_source=affiliate_ir_Adpump&irmptype=mediapartner&ircid=7385&iradname=Homepage%3A+EN%28US%29+GoEuro&utm_id=274922&subId1=&gad_source=1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer sponsored" class="text-[#69746E] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#4a534f]">Omio</a>, as it lets you compare different train options in one place. If you're travelling on a budget, it's also worth checking whether <a href="https://global.flixbus.com/bus" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer sponsored" class="text-[#69746E] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#4a534f]">FlixBus</a> operates on your route.</p>
      <p>Once you arrive at Bruges train station, the historic centre is about a 20-minute walk away. If you're travelling with luggage, you can also take a taxi or use a local bus to reach your accommodation.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="faq-1" class="scroll-mt-nav">
      <h4 class="mb-2 text-black">2. What is the best time to visit Bruges?</h4>
      <p>Bruges is a beautiful destination year-round, and the best time to visit really depends on the kind of experience you're looking for. Spring (April–June) and early autumn (September–October) are ideal if you prefer pleasant weather and fewer crowds, while winter brings a magical atmosphere with festive lights and Christmas decorations.</p>
      <p>I visited during the Christmas season, and the Christmas atmosphere made the city feel even more magical. If you're planning a winter trip, Bruges at Christmas is something I'd happily recommend.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="faq-2" class="scroll-mt-nav">
      <h4 class="mb-2 text-black">3. How many days do you need in Bruges?</h4>
      <p>I'd recommend spending 2 days in Bruges. You can see the main attractions in a single day, but I think you'd be missing part of what makes the city so special. Having an extra day lets you slow down, revisit your favourite places, and enjoy Bruges without feeling like you're constantly checking your watch.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="faq-3" class="scroll-mt-nav">
      <h4 class="mb-2 text-black">4. Is Bruges worth visiting?</h4>
      <p>Absolutely. If you enjoy historic cities, canals, beautiful architecture, and exploring on foot, Bruges is one of the most charming destinations in Europe. What I loved most about Bruges is that you don't need to rush from one attraction to another — some of my favourite moments were simply walking around, discovering quiet streets, stopping by the canals, and finding beautiful corners along the way.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="section-12" class="scroll-mt-nav">
  <div class={prose}>
    <ArticleClosingNote label="Before you go">
      <p>I hope this guide helps you plan an unforgettable first visit to Bruges. And who knows? Maybe, like me, you'll already be thinking about coming back before you even leave.</p>
    </ArticleClosingNote>
  </div>
</section>
